## Project Overview

This project analyzes HCAHPS healthcare data to understand patient experience and hospital performance across time, geography, and patient-experience dimensions.

The solution brings together multiple related datasets and applies data preparation, relational modeling, DAX-based analytics, interactive visualization, and Power BI Q&A to produce an interactive analytical dashboard.

| Area | Details |
|---|---|
| **Domain** | Healthcare / Patient Experience |
| **BI Platform** | Microsoft Power BI |
| **Data Preparation** | Power Query |
| **Transformation** | M Query |
| **Analytical Layer** | DAX |
| **Data Model** | Star Schema |
| **Analysis Period** | 2015–2023 |
| **Geographic Level** | National, Regional & State |
| **Primary Metric** | Top-Box Percentage |
| **AI Feature** | Power BI Q&A |

---

## Business Problem

HCAHPS data contains multiple measures that describe different aspects of the patient experience. These measures can vary across reporting periods, states, and regions.

The project was designed to answer the following analytical questions:

- How has overall hospital performance changed over time?
- How does Overall Hospital Rating compare with Willingness to Recommend?
- Which patient-experience dimensions perform strongly or weakly?
- How does Overall Hospital Rating vary across states?
- How does reported survey response rate vary across regions and states?
- How has Top-Box performance changed between 2015 and 2023?

---

## Business Objectives

- Evaluate overall patient-experience performance
- Monitor Overall Hospital Rating
- Analyze Willingness to Recommend
- Compare patient-experience dimensions
- Track performance across reporting periods
- Identify state-level variation
- Explore regional differences
- Analyze reported survey response rates
- Compare Top-Box performance between 2015 and 2023
- Provide an interactive analytical solution for performance exploration

---

## Key Performance Indicators

<div align="center">

| KPI | 2023 |
|:---|---:|
| **Overall Hospital Rating Top Box** | **70%** |
| **Willingness to Recommend Top Box** | **69%** |
| **Historical Peak Overall Hospital Rating** | **73%** |

</div>

The two primary KPIs provide a high-level view of overall patient perception and willingness to recommend.

The historical peak is used as a benchmark for evaluating current Overall Hospital Rating performance.

---

## 2023 Patient Experience Performance

The dashboard compares eight supporting patient-experience measures using their Top-Box percentages.

| Measure | Top-Box Performance |
|:---|---:|
| **Discharge Information** | **86%** |
| Communication with Doctors | 79% |
| Communication with Nurses | 79% |
| Cleanliness | 72% |
| Responsiveness | 65% |
| Quietness | 62% |
| Communication about Medicines | 61% |
| **Care Transition** | **51%** |

Overall Hospital Rating and Willingness to Recommend are treated separately as headline indicators.

---

## Dataset

The project uses seven related HCAHPS tables.

| Table | Rows | Columns | Purpose |
|:---|---:|---:|:---|
| **Reports** | 9 | 4 | Reporting periods and dates |
| **States** | 56 | 3 | State names, state codes, and regions |
| **Measures** | 10 | 3 | HCAHPS patient-experience measures |
| **Questions** | 19 | 6 | Survey questions mapped to measures |
| **National Results** | 90 | 8 | National Bottom-, Middle-, and Top-Box results |
| **State Results** | 4,580 | 9 | State-level results across measures and periods |
| **Responses** | 43,219 | 5 | Facility survey counts and reported response rates |

The source tables were maintained separately because they represent different analytical grains and serve different roles within the Power BI model.

---

## Data Preparation

Data preparation was performed using **Power Query**.

### Key Transformations

| Transformation | Purpose |
|:---|:---|
| **Promote Headers** | Converted source rows into column headers |
| **Change Data Types** | Assigned appropriate data types to analytical fields |
| **Response Rate Transformation** | Created a numeric response-rate field while handling non-numeric values |
| **Percentage Validation** | Validated Bottom-, Middle-, and Top-Box percentage distributions |
| **Facility ID Preservation** | Kept Facility ID as Text to preserve alphanumeric identifiers and leading zeros |

### Response Rate

The original response-rate field contained both numeric and non-numeric values.

A separate numeric field was created so that valid response-rate values could be analyzed without incorrectly converting unavailable values.

